WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.400
I'm Jenna Fisher, and I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是詹娜·费舍尔，我是安吉拉·金西。

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.240
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.380
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你带来终极的《办公室》粉丝播客。

4
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.360
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office
每周，我们将深入探索《办公室》的世界

5
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:21.080
with exclusive interviews, behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
带来独家访谈、幕后花絮以及大量闺蜜故事。

6
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.100
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0版。

7
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.400
Hi there, Angela.
嗨，安吉拉。

8
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.400
Hey, good morning.
嘿，早安。

9
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:28.360
Good morning.
早安。

10
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:34.520
You were telling me a tale as I was warming up my coffee this morning about your mascara.
今天早上我热咖啡的时候，你跟我讲了一个关于你睫毛膏的故事。

11
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.120
Well, here's the thing.
是这样的。

12
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:41.580
I walked in, said good morning to Sam, good morning to Jenna, hi to Matt on Zoom.
我走进来，跟萨姆说了早安，跟詹娜说了早安，在Zoom上跟马特打了招呼。

13
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.580
I go to use the restroom.
我去上洗手间。

14
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.120
I have a massive mascara clump on my cheek.
我脸颊上有一大团结块的睫毛膏。

15
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:46.400
Nobody.
竟然没人告诉我。

16
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:47.600
I didn't know.
我根本不知道。

17
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.940
I was in my own world getting my coffee ready.
我当时沉浸在自己的世界里准备咖啡。

18
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:50.820
Did you know?
你知道吗？

19
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.040
No, apparently I didn't look up for my phone when you came in.
不，显然你进来的时候我正低头看手机。

20
00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:53.720
Apparently not.
显然是的。

21
00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.120
But also, I guess Josh didn't notice when I said goodbye to him.
不过话说回来，我跟乔什道别时，他好像也没注意到。

22
00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:59.300
I always give him a kiss goodbye.
我每次走都会亲吻他告别。

23
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.920
No, giant black clump of mascara on my cheek.
天呐，我脸颊上有一大团黑色的睫毛膏。

24
00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.800
But pretty much this morning has been a little bit of a get-ready fail.
总之今天早上我有点诸事不顺。

25
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.640
I slept with my hair wet, so you know what I woke up to.
我湿着头发睡觉，所以你知道我醒来时是什么德行。

26
00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.260
Your hair looks great for having slept with it wet.
以湿发睡觉的标准来看，你的头发看起来真不错。

27
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.180
Well, I tried to tame my hair all morning.
好吧，我整个早上都在努力驯服我的头发。

28
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.040
It looks great.
看起来真的很棒。

29
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.300
Oh, it's underneath.
哦，那是在下面。

30
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.320
Don't look at the back.
别看后面。

31
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.160
Okay, whatever.
好吧，管他呢。

32
00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:17.840
Let it go.
算了吧。

33
00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.860
Let go of the back of my head a long time ago.
我早就放弃管我脑勺后面的头发了。

34
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:26.160
But then also, I will hold on to makeup way past the time you're supposed to hold on to it.
但还有一件事，我用化妆品的时间总是远远超过它的使用期限。

35
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.800
Like my powder compact right now is just one tiny square that's left.
比如我现在的粉饼，就只剩一小方块了。

36
00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.340
Most of it is broken off.
大部分都碎掉了。

37
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.980
And then I will smush what's left of the powder.
然后我会把剩下的粉末拼命挤压在一起。

38
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.780
And then, like, I'm not throwing that away.
反正就是舍不得扔掉。

39
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.460
Well, I was doing this with my blush as well.
我用腮红的时候也是这样。

40
00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:47.080
And I had dropped it once, so I had a crack through it.
我以前摔过一次，所以上面有一道裂纹。

41
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.240
And it was getting a little precarious, but I still kept finding a way to use it.
虽然已经有点摇摇欲坠了，但我还是想方设法继续用它。

42
00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.360
And this morning, I'm rushing because my hair is crazy.
今天早上，因为头发太乱我很赶时间。

43
00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.260
And I grabbed that blush out of the drawer.
我从抽屉里抓起那盒腮红。

44
00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.300
And I open it.
然后我打开它。

45
00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.220
And all the inside of it has crumbled like a fine paper.
结果里面所有的东西都像碎纸屑一样碎掉了。

46
00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.560
And it went all over.
弄得到处都是。

47
00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.440
What are you just, like, blush confetti?
你这是弄成了腮红纸屑雨吗？

48
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.760
All over the sink, all over the counter.
水槽到处都是，柜台到处都是。

49
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.400
I had to change my top.
我不得不换了件上衣。

50
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.080
So I don't know what the lesson is, you guys.
所以各位，我也不知道这能说明什么道理。

51
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.780
Maybe just, like, when things are past their due date, let them go.
也许只是，比如说，当东西过了保质期，就随它去吧。

52
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:24.180
You know, this sounds like my New Year's resolution about, like, little fixes, big wins.
你知道，这听起来像我关于那种小调整、大收获的新年决心。

53
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:24.800
Yeah.
对。

54
00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.940
Like, if you fix that problem, then it won't explode on you later.
比如说，如果你解决了那个问题，它以后就不会突然爆发了。

55
00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.180
Later, maybe it's okay to toss that very old blush.
过会儿，也许把那个很旧的腮红扔了也行。

56
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.720
I think it's three years old.
我觉得它已经三年了。

57
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.080
Well, you know, lady, my problem is that now I can barely see without my glasses.
好吧，你知道，女士，我的问题是现在我不戴眼镜几乎什么都看不清。

58
00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.900
I cannot read at all.
我简直没法阅读。

59
00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.120
You know, I already worry about the apocalypse.
你知道的，我已经开始担心末日了。

60
00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:45.660
Sure.
当然。

61
00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.580
I'm worried that I'm going to lose my glasses during the apocalypse.
我担心在末日的时候我会把眼镜弄丢。

62
00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.180
And then I'm not even going to be able to read a book during it.
然后到时候我连书都读不成了。

63
00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.140
Oh, that'd be horrible.
哦，那太可怕了。

64
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:52.920
Can you imagine?
你能想象吗？

65
00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:53.340
No.
不能。

66
00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.120
I worry that I'm going to be barefoot during the apocalypse.
我担心在末日时我会光着脚。

67
00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.260
And it's going to be like Die Hard, where he's running around barefoot,
就像《虎胆龙威》那样，他在里面光着脚跑来跑去，

68
00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.000
trying to fight the bad guys.
试图与坏人搏斗。

69
00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.360
This is another one of my worries.
这是我的另一个担忧。

70
00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:02.760
Yes.
是的。

71
00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:03.700
Shoes and glasses.
鞋子和眼镜。

72
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:04.400
Very important.
非常重要。

73
00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.460
Well, I can't see my face when I put my makeup on anymore.
好吧，我现在化妆时都看不清自己的脸了。

74
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.600
And it doesn't matter if I use one of those magnifying mirror things.
而且不管我用不用那种放大镜都没用。

75
00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.260
It's not enough magnification.
放大倍数根本不够。

76
00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:20.560
So every morning when I do my makeup, then I put my glasses on and I see what I've done.
所以每天早上我化完妆，然后戴上眼镜，看看自己都画成了什么样。

77
00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.260
And it's never great.
而且从来都没好看到哪里去。

78
00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.560
Do you have to tone it down?
你得下手轻一点吗？

79
00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.520
It's not the toning it down.
倒不是下手轻不轻的问题。

80
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.620
It's that like the eyeliner isn't in any way straight.
而是眼线根本就画不直。

81
00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.580
It looks straight to me when I put it on in a blur.
在我模模糊糊画的时候，我觉得挺直的。

82
00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:38.960
Or I will have like gobs of mascara underneath my eye and I can't see them until I put my glasses on.
或者我眼睛下面会有一团团的睫毛膏，在戴上眼镜之前我都看不见。

83
00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.900
So I have to do my makeup, then put my glasses on,
所以我得先化好妆，再戴上眼镜，

84
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.860
and then go in with like a wet Q-tip and like fix everything.
然后拿一根湿棉签去把所有地方修正好。

85
00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.580
I wonder what we're going to look like when we're old ladies.
我在想我们老了以后会是什么样子。

86
00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.760
Like legit old ladies.
真正的老太太那种。

87
00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.560
Like I think I'm going to have too much blush.
比如我觉得我以后会涂太多腮红。

88
00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:52.120
Yeah.
对。

89
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.580
Too much blush, too much lip.
腮红太多，口红太多。

90
00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.140
And you're going to have like a lot of mascara globs.
而你呢，会有很多结块的睫毛膏。

91
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:56.700
Yeah.
对。

92
00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.360
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

93
00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.080
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

94
00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.640
I feel the same way.
我也是这种感觉。

95
00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.260
I don't mind.
我倒不介意。

96
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:03.560
All right.
好吧。

97
00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:06.980
Should we get into our fan chit chat question of the week?
我们要不要开始本周的粉丝闲聊问题？

98
00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:07.620
Yes.
好的。

99
00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.380
Should we also say what we're here to discuss today?
我们要不要也说说今天来这儿要讨论什么？

100
00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:11.500
I mean, we can.
我是说，可以啊。

101
00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.060
You guys, we're going to get to it.
各位，我们马上就要开始了。

102
00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.380
We're doing episode nine of the paper.
我们要讲的是《办公室》的第九集。

103
00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.920
It's called Matching Ponchos.
这集叫做《同款斗篷》。

104
00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.820
But first, let's have a chit chat.
但在那之前，我们先闲聊一会儿。

105
00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.020
This one's coming to us from Alexander G.
这条留言来自德克萨斯州大学城的亚历山大·G。

106
00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.780
in College Station, Texas.
位于德克萨斯州大学城。

107
00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.680
Howdy, Jenna and Angela.
珍娜和安吉拉，你们好。

108
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.640
I'm Alexander G.
我是来自德克萨斯州大学城的亚历山大·G。

109
00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.300
from College Station, Texas.
我是来自德克萨斯州大学城的亚历山大·G。

110
00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:35.240
My question for you guys is, if you guys have not pursued acting,
我给你们的问题是，如果你们当初没有追求演艺事业，

111
00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.660
what would y'all's career be?
你们会选择什么职业？

112
00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:42.900
I'm very curious to know you guys' answer to this question.
我很想知道你们对这个问题的答案。

113
00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:44.680
And love the pod.
并且很喜欢这个播客。

114
00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:45.500
Thank you, guys.
谢谢你们，伙计们。

115
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:46.600
All right.
好的。

116
00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.440
Thank you, Alexander.
谢谢你，亚历山大。

117
00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.160
I know.
我知道。

118
00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:49.980
I thought that was such a thoughtful question.
我觉得这是一个非常深思熟虑的问题。

119
00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.060
I've thought about this.
我考虑过这件事。

120
00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:52.460
Yeah?
是吗？

121
00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.300
I know my answer.
我知道我的答案。

122
00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:55.780
Well, you should go.
好吧，你先说。

123
00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.860
I think I would be a vet tech.
我想我会成为一名兽医助理。

124
00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:00.080
Oh, you'd be such a great vet tech.
哦，你会是个非常出色的兽医助理。

125
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.060
You have such a heart for animals, Jenna.
珍娜，你对动物太有爱心了。

126
00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:03.080
Yeah.
对啊。

127
00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:06.860
I mean, those were the two choices I was weighing when I was younger.
我的意思是，那是我年轻时在权衡的两种选择。

128
00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.900
I thought, do I want to become a veterinarian?
我想，我是想成为一名兽医？

129
00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.820
Do I want to become a vet tech?
还是想成为一名兽医助理？

130
00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.100
Do I want to become an actor?
还是想成为一名演员？

131
00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.760
Right before I got my job on the office,
就在我得到《办公室》的工作之前，

132
00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.680
I had just started doing rescue work with Kitten Rescue.
我刚刚开始在“小猫救援”组织做救援工作。

133
00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.780
And they teach you, like, a lot of vet tech kind of stuff, you know, giving medications,
他们会教你很多兽医助理相关的技能，你知道的，比如喂药、

134
00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:29.000
giving fluids, giving vaccines, being able to spot illnesses, things like that.
输液、打疫苗、识别疾病之类的。

135
00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.940
There's a lot of that in the rescue stuff.
救援工作里有很多这样的内容。

136
00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.060
And I really loved it.
而且我真的很喜欢。

137
00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.420
So I called my manager, Naomi, and my acting coach, Robert.
所以我给我的经纪人娜奥米和我的表演教练罗伯特打了电话。

138
00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.700
And I said, you guys, I think I might want to make a change.
我说，伙计们，我想我可能想做出改变了。

139
00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:43.620
If something doesn't happen this pilot season, I think I want to take some time off.
如果在这次试播季期间没有起色，我想休息一段时间。

140
00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.680
I want to go to two years of vet tech school.
我想去读两年制的兽医助理学校。

141
00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:52.880
I just, the acting thing is feeling like just eight years of rejection.
我只是觉得，演艺事业感觉就像是长达八年的拒绝。

142
00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:57.520
Like, I'm just like, it has worn me down.
就好像，我真的被它折磨得精疲力竭了。

143
00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.240
Yeah, it can be a real beat down.
是的，这真的很打击人。

144
00:05:59.560 --> 00:05:59.920
Yeah.
是啊。

145
00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:03.420
And this other thing is giving me purpose.
而另一件事给了我目标。

146
00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:05.340
It's making me feel joyful.
它让我感到快乐。

147
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:06.900
I feel needed.
我感到了被需要。

148
00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.560
And I feel good at it.
而且我觉得我很擅长这个。

149
00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.460
And I want to pursue that.
我想去追求这个。

150
00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.580
And then I'll know, like, should I go back to acting?
然后我就会知道，我是不是该回去演戏？

151
00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:15.540
But I might need to take like a sabbatical.
但我可能需要休假一段时间。

152
00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.460
Well, as we know, I ended up going out for the office.
嗯，正如我们所知，我最后去试镜了《办公室》。

153
00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:21.020
And then everything sort of changed.
然后一切都变了。

154
00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:22.920
And that path was the one chosen for me.
那条路是为我选定的。

155
00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.400
But I've continued to do the animal rescue work.
但我一直在继续动物救援工作。

156
00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.300
I mean, I'm fostering kittens right now.
我是说，我现在正在寄养小猫。

157
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:31.460
I mean, that's one of the first things I learned about you in our friendship.
我的意思是，这是我们在建立友谊时我最先了解你的事情之一。

158
