778
00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:29.180
Was that your experience, Jenna?
珍娜，你也是这种体验吗？

779
00:33:29.460 --> 00:33:33.280
Well, he's calling them plates because that's the industry term, but I think it's more accurate
嗯，他称之为“片状装置”，因为这是行业术语，但我认为

780
00:33:33.280 --> 00:33:37.260
to say they're like giant green screens that surround the car.
更准确的说法是它们就像环绕汽车的巨型绿幕。

781
00:33:37.480 --> 00:33:45.620
And then they project the road onto it, the moving road onto these screens that surround the car.
然后他们把道路投影上去，把运动的道路投影到环绕汽车的这些屏幕上。

782
00:33:45.620 --> 00:33:50.660
Yeah, there were like these huge squares on stands that surround the car.
对，就像是环绕汽车的立在支架上的那些巨大方块。

783
00:33:50.820 --> 00:33:51.000
Yeah.
对。

784
00:33:51.240 --> 00:33:56.000
And then they can put whatever they want on those big squares to show wherever you are.
然后他们可以在这些大方块上显示任何他们想要的内容，来展示你所在的地点。

785
00:33:56.180 --> 00:33:59.920
So my driving scene was in a city, they're in the country.
所以我的开车戏是在城市里，而他们在乡村。

786
00:34:00.480 --> 00:34:04.720
Yeah, I did this for that television show I did in London called You, Me, and the Apocalypse.
对，我在伦敦拍的那部叫《你、我与世界末日》的电视剧里也这样做过。

787
00:34:06.060 --> 00:34:11.040
And it was crazy because like in this episode, there's going to be a moment where like Donal
这太疯狂了，因为在这集里，会有一个时刻，比如唐纳

788
00:34:11.040 --> 00:34:13.760
puts the window down, Ned puts the window down.
摇下车窗，内德摇下车窗。

789
00:34:13.760 --> 00:34:15.760
And then like all this air comes in.
然后就会有大量的风吹进来。

790
00:34:15.900 --> 00:34:19.140
And so they have, it's like old timey fans.
所以他们备有那种老式风扇。

791
00:34:19.520 --> 00:34:24.600
And also like truly there's just some dudes in the back just like rocking the car.
而且真的还有几个大汉在后面晃动汽车。

792
00:34:24.800 --> 00:34:29.080
Yeah, I did find it kind of surreal because I'd only ever done driving scenes on the office
对，我确实觉得这有点超现实，因为我以前只在《办公室》里拍过开车戏，

793
00:34:29.080 --> 00:34:30.480
where we were actually on the road.
当时我们是真的在路上开。

794
00:34:30.500 --> 00:34:34.460
So the things I looked out the window were real trees I was passing and stuff like that.
所以透过窗户看到的都是我路过的真实树木之类的东西。

795
00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:38.300
And when I did my scene on Better Things, I'm in the back seat and we hit a bump.
而当我拍摄《美好的事情》那场戏时，我坐在后座，我们压到一个坎。

796
00:34:38.800 --> 00:34:42.440
But it's kind of distracting because there's just like three men right outside.
但这有点让人分心，因为外面刚好有三个大男人。

797
00:34:42.840 --> 00:34:43.000
Yeah.
对。

798
00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:44.820
Like kind of raising the car.
就像是在把车抬起来一样。

799
00:34:45.760 --> 00:34:45.840
Yeah.
对。

800
00:34:45.940 --> 00:34:50.180
David said while there are pros and cons to using this technique, ultimately he felt like
大卫说，虽然使用这种技术有利有弊，但他最终觉得

801
00:34:50.180 --> 00:34:53.260
it looked pretty realistic and allowed them to have more shooting time.
这看起来相当逼真，并且让他们有了更多的拍摄时间。

802
00:34:53.300 --> 00:34:55.480
And that took away a lot of pressure for everyone.
这为每个人减轻了很大的压力。

803
00:34:55.720 --> 00:34:57.780
And I think you see them having fun.
而且我觉得你能看出他们玩得很开心。

804
00:34:58.200 --> 00:34:59.920
I think it really paid off.
我认为这真的很值得。

805
00:35:00.160 --> 00:35:01.260
They tricked me.
他们把我骗了。

806
00:35:01.760 --> 00:35:04.760
So I watched it and my question was the same.
所以我看了，我的问题也是一样的。

807
00:35:04.880 --> 00:35:06.220
Where did they do these driving scenes?
这些驾驶场景是在哪拍的？

808
00:35:06.420 --> 00:35:09.560
And when we got this information from Dave, I went back and re-watched it.
当我们从戴夫那里得到这个消息时，我回去重新看了一遍。

809
00:35:09.740 --> 00:35:11.720
I can't tell at all.
我完全看不出来。

810
00:35:12.040 --> 00:35:12.360
Same.
我也是。

811
00:35:12.520 --> 00:35:16.540
I literally thought they took a road trip to like some part of Northern California where
我真的以为他们开车去了一趟北加州之类的什么地方

812
00:35:16.540 --> 00:35:17.520
it's farming community.
那里是个农业社区。

813
00:35:17.620 --> 00:35:17.940
Same.
我也是。

814
00:35:18.420 --> 00:35:24.120
Well, I had another question for Dave about how they shot these scenes, especially now
对了，我还有一个关于戴夫的问题，问他们是怎么拍这些场景的，尤其是现在

815
00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:25.820
knowing that they weren't really on the road.
知道了他们其实根本不在路上之后。

816
00:35:26.260 --> 00:35:28.500
You know, Ange, my family is re-watching The Office.
你知道的，安吉，我家人正在重温《办公室》。

817
00:35:29.140 --> 00:35:31.140
It's my kid's first time seeing the show.
这是我孩子第一次看这部剧。

818
00:35:31.980 --> 00:35:33.180
It's been really fun.
真的很有趣。

819
00:35:33.340 --> 00:35:38.480
But something I'm noticing is how when we had driving scenes on The Office, you know,
但我注意到的一点是，当我们在《办公室》里有驾驶场景时，你知道的

820
00:35:38.560 --> 00:35:41.080
we use the little lipstick cameras inside the car.
我们在车里用的是小型口红摄像机。

821
00:35:41.360 --> 00:35:41.520
Yeah.
是的。

822
00:35:41.860 --> 00:35:44.040
There is a real degrade in quality.
画质真的有很大程度的下降。

823
00:35:44.420 --> 00:35:49.040
Like if you see us in the office and then it cuts to people in the car, I didn't really
就像如果你看到我们在办公室里，然后镜头切到车里的人，我以前真的

824
00:35:49.040 --> 00:35:52.100
notice it before, like originally when I watched the show.
没有注意到，比如最初我看这部剧的时候。

825
00:35:52.260 --> 00:35:54.440
But now in this re-watch, I'm really seeing it.
但现在这次重温时，我真的看出来了。

826
00:35:54.620 --> 00:35:58.460
And I asked Dave, like, this looks really clear.
我问戴夫，这看起来真的很清晰。

827
00:35:58.460 --> 00:36:01.520
Like, I'm not seeing that degrade in quality.
就是说，我没有看到那种画质下降。

828
00:36:01.720 --> 00:36:03.260
Were you using lipstick cameras?
你们当时用的是口红摄像机吗？

829
00:36:03.440 --> 00:36:04.560
Like, how did that work?
这是怎么运作的？

830
00:36:05.080 --> 00:36:10.220
And Dave said that the lipstick cameras that we use in the cars shooting The Office, they
戴夫说，我们在拍《办公室》时车里用的口红摄像机，它们

831
00:36:10.220 --> 00:36:14.580
did not have the same quality of resolution or lenses that our regular cameras had.
没有我们常规摄像机那样的分辨率或镜头质量。

832
00:36:14.820 --> 00:36:18.120
He said, but that was the style for documentaries back then.
他说，但那是当时纪录片的风格。

833
00:36:18.240 --> 00:36:21.580
That was what happened on reality shows when you got in the car.
那正是真人秀节目里你上车时会发生的情况。

834
00:36:21.580 --> 00:36:24.380
And that they sort of saw that as part of the storytelling.
而且他们某种程度上将这视作叙事的一部分。

835
00:36:24.620 --> 00:36:25.280
They liked it.
他们喜欢这样。

836
00:36:25.540 --> 00:36:25.760
Yeah.
是的。

837
00:36:25.960 --> 00:36:26.800
They embraced it.
他们欣然接受了这一点。

838
00:36:27.680 --> 00:36:31.740
He said, but now, you know, we're several years from The Office ending and he believes
他说，不过现在，你知道的，距离《办公室》剧终已经过去好几年了，他相信

839
00:36:31.740 --> 00:36:33.860
the documentary crew got some newer equipment.
纪录片摄制组换了一些更新的设备。

840
00:36:34.520 --> 00:36:40.000
They still use lipstick cameras, but now lipstick cameras can get you a sharper image.
他们仍然在使用口红摄像机，但现在的口红摄像机能为你带来更清晰的画面。

841
00:36:40.280 --> 00:36:41.520
And listen to this.
听听这个。

842
00:36:41.700 --> 00:36:43.600
They can be controlled remotely.
它们可以被远程控制。

843
00:36:43.640 --> 00:36:44.800
You can zoom.
你可以变焦。

844
00:36:45.120 --> 00:36:45.920
You can pan.
你可以摇镜头。

845
00:36:46.280 --> 00:36:48.140
We couldn't do any of that stuff.
我们以前可做不到这些。

846
00:36:48.540 --> 00:36:50.960
Our lipstick cameras were fixed in one place.
我们的口红摄像机是固定在一个地方的。

847
00:36:50.960 --> 00:36:51.900
That's all you got.
你就只能得到那些。

848
00:36:52.120 --> 00:36:53.980
And you only saw what their lens saw.
而且你只能看到它们的镜头所捕捉到的画面。

849
00:36:54.140 --> 00:36:58.680
So he said they used three in the car, but they could pan.
所以他说他们在车里用了三个，但它们可以摇镜。

850
00:36:58.880 --> 00:36:59.520
They could zoom.
它们可以变焦。

851
00:36:59.720 --> 00:37:00.880
He said it was amazing.
他说这太棒了。

852
00:37:01.260 --> 00:37:06.220
He said he positioned one as a wide shot and then he did two that kind of were cross-angled.
他说他把其中一台设为全景镜头，然后又拍了两个交叉角度的镜头。

853
00:37:06.460 --> 00:37:10.320
He wanted to be able to see the actors, but he also wanted to see out the side windows.
他既想能看到演员，又想能看到侧窗外面。

854
00:37:11.580 --> 00:37:12.920
Well, you got me.
好吧，你把我问住了。

855
00:37:13.100 --> 00:37:14.280
I thought it was amazing.
我觉得这太棒了。

856
00:37:14.480 --> 00:37:15.220
Really well done.
真的做得很好。

857
00:37:15.680 --> 00:37:19.800
Well, now we go back to the Toledo truth teller in the bullpen.
好了，现在我们回到办公室里的托莱多真话大王。

858
00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:24.280
And Oscar is really spinning out over being called an asshat.
而奥斯卡听到自己被叫作“混蛋”后，整个人彻底抓狂了。

859
00:37:24.780 --> 00:37:26.820
And he has a rant.
他开始大发牢骚。

860
00:37:27.020 --> 00:37:32.160
Jenna and I both texted Oscar Nunez about how amazing he is in this rant.
珍娜和我都给奥斯卡·努涅斯发了信息，称赞他在这一段里的表现简直棒极了。

861
00:37:32.420 --> 00:37:36.080
I mean, eventually he's going to come on and we're going to talk to him all about it.
我的意思是，他迟早会来节目，我们会跟他好好聊聊这件事。

862
00:37:36.220 --> 00:37:39.180
But this was my chef's kiss moment of the episode.
但这是我心目中这一集的神来之笔。

863
00:37:39.360 --> 00:37:39.420
Yeah.
对。

864
00:37:39.420 --> 00:37:40.500
I think we should hear it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

865
00:37:41.340 --> 00:37:44.060
Oscar, do you have the order number for...
奥斯卡，你有……的订单号吗？

866
00:37:44.060 --> 00:37:47.320
Asshat is just such an unforgivably stupid word.
“混蛋”这个词真是蠢得无可救药。

867
00:37:47.520 --> 00:37:47.880
Unforgivably?
无可救药？

868
00:37:48.220 --> 00:37:49.100
Another adverb.
又是一个副词。

869
00:37:49.340 --> 00:37:51.120
Okay, well, it's a vile thing to call someone.
好吧，骂别人这种话太恶劣了。

870
00:37:51.240 --> 00:37:53.920
But all I'm saying is how stupid it is.
但我只想说这个词有多蠢。

871
00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:54.700
Because what?
因为什么？

872
00:37:54.840 --> 00:37:56.160
So in this scenario, what?
所以在这种情况下，什么意思？

873
00:37:56.300 --> 00:37:58.180
I'm a little hat worn by an ass?
我是驴子戴的小帽子吗？

874
00:37:58.400 --> 00:37:59.500
An ass wears a hat?
驴子戴帽子？

875
00:38:00.840 --> 00:38:03.040
Or am I an ass-shaped hat?
还是说我是一顶驴子形状的帽子？

876
00:38:03.260 --> 00:38:03.580
What?
什么？

877
00:38:03.980 --> 00:38:05.140
Do you see what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

878
00:38:06.300 --> 00:38:07.740
I want to find them.
我想找到他们。

879
00:38:07.860 --> 00:38:10.740
I want to find them and grab them.
我想找到他们并抓住他们。

880
00:38:10.900 --> 00:38:16.340
And just explain to them how funny it is.
然后向他们解释这有多搞笑。

881
00:38:16.480 --> 00:38:18.640
The whole scenario, how amusing it is to me.
整个状况，这对我来说有多好笑。

882
00:38:18.960 --> 00:38:19.440
That's all.
就这些。

883
00:38:20.180 --> 00:38:21.080
Because you can't.
因为你不能。

884
00:38:21.100 --> 00:38:21.600
But you can't.
但你就是不能。

885
00:38:21.680 --> 00:38:24.780
Because it's computers and it's internet.
因为这是电脑，这是互联网。

886
00:38:25.040 --> 00:38:27.260
So you can't tell them because you can't find them because there's no way to...
所以你没法告诉他们，因为你找不到他们，因为根本没办法……

887
00:38:27.260 --> 00:38:28.660
You can track down their IP address.
你可以追踪他们的IP地址。

888
00:38:29.480 --> 00:38:30.280
IP address?
IP地址？

889
00:38:30.500 --> 00:38:30.820
Yeah.
对。

890
00:38:31.280 --> 00:38:31.900
It's traceable.
这是可追踪的。

891
00:38:31.980 --> 00:38:32.640
I can track them.
我可以追踪他们。

892
00:38:32.660 --> 00:38:33.680
Oh, no, no.
哦，不，不。

893
00:38:33.900 --> 00:38:35.040
Oscar, look at me, dude.
奥斯卡，看着我，老兄。

894
00:38:36.960 --> 00:38:38.760
It can be surprisingly expensive.
这可能会贵得惊人。

895
00:38:39.080 --> 00:38:45.260
Okay, but if you do want to go down this road, you'd call IT and the number is 3-2-7-1.
好吧，但如果你真的想走这条路，你可以打电话给IT部门，号码是3-2-7-1。

896
00:38:46.880 --> 00:38:49.660
Lady, I love the journey that Oscar goes on.
天哪，我太喜欢奥斯卡的心路历程了。

897
00:38:49.900 --> 00:38:52.140
He's angry, but then he's like, but it's funny.
他很生气，但接着他又觉得，不过这挺搞笑的。

898
00:38:52.240 --> 00:38:53.080
It's funny to me.
我觉得这挺好笑的。

899
00:38:53.220 --> 00:38:53.400
Yeah.
对。

900
00:38:53.620 --> 00:38:57.220
And then also a little bit that this dates all of us.
然后还有一点，这件事暴露了我们的年龄。

901
00:38:57.460 --> 00:38:59.920
We're of a certain generation that you're like, but you can't find it.
我们属于那种特定的一代人，你会觉得，但你就是找不到它。

902
00:39:00.040 --> 00:39:00.620
It's computers.
是电脑。

903
00:39:00.940 --> 00:39:01.160
Yeah.
对。

904
00:39:01.460 --> 00:39:02.780
There's no way you'll ever know.
你根本不可能知道。

905
00:39:03.480 --> 00:39:07.300
And they're like, actually, it's just, you can track down the IP address.
而他们却说，其实，很简单，你可以追踪到IP地址。

906
00:39:08.160 --> 00:39:15.180
We should mention that Oscar was nominated for a Critics' Choice Award for the paper for Best Supporting Actor in a Comedy.
我们应该提一下，奥斯卡曾因该报纸获得评论家选择奖喜剧类最佳男配角提名。

907
00:39:15.520 --> 00:39:17.500
And this is why, guys.
这就是原因，各位。

908
00:39:17.920 --> 00:39:19.440
This is it right here.
就是这个。

909
00:39:19.580 --> 00:39:20.540
Watch this scene.
看这个场景。

910
00:39:20.920 --> 00:39:26.800
He does this very funny thing, too, where he does like a little tiny hat like on his head.
他还有一个非常搞笑的举动，就是把一顶小帽子戴在头上。

911
00:39:26.800 --> 00:39:28.620
He's like, am I an ass and wears a hat?
他好像在说，我戴着帽子是个混蛋吗？

912
00:39:29.440 --> 00:39:30.260
It's great.
太棒了。

913
00:39:30.440 --> 00:39:31.480
Oscar is just brilliant.
奥斯卡实在太才华横溢了。

914
00:39:32.040 --> 00:39:33.460
Well, why don't we take a break?
好了，我们为什么不休息一下呢？

915
00:39:33.460 --> 00:39:37.060
And when we come back, there is a spider in Mare's car.
等我们回来时，梅尔的车里有一只蜘蛛。

916
00:39:38.660 --> 00:39:39.360
I'm sorry.
对不起。

917
00:39:39.480 --> 00:39:40.220
I'm laughing about it.
我在笑这件事。

918
00:39:40.240 --> 00:39:40.620
I know.
我知道。

919
00:39:40.820 --> 00:39:41.980
Because it's so good.
因为太精彩了。

920
00:39:42.060 --> 00:39:43.580
I watched this scene so many times.
这个场景我看了好多次。

921
00:39:43.940 --> 00:39:45.220
We need to break it down.
我们需要剖析一下。

922
00:39:45.380 --> 00:39:45.960
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

923
00:39:55.870 --> 00:40:00.630
We are back, and it's time for Around the Town.
我们回来了，现在是“走遍全城”时间。

924
00:40:02.700 --> 00:40:04.960
Our first one is from Sarah T.
我们的第一个问题来自威斯康星州伯灵顿的莎拉·T。

925
00:40:05.160 --> 00:40:06.580
in Burlington, Wisconsin.
来自威斯康星州伯灵顿。

926
00:40:07.420 --> 00:40:13.800
Sarah wrote in and said, every winter, my town puts an old car on the ice of the lake downtown.
莎拉来信说，每年冬天，我们镇上都会把一辆旧车放在市中心湖泊的冰面上。

927
00:40:14.580 --> 00:40:18.560
There is a contest for whoever can guess the day it falls through the ice.
有一个比赛，看谁能猜中它掉进冰窟窿的那一天。

928
00:40:18.740 --> 00:40:21.060
It just recently made its yearly appearance.
它最近刚刚完成了每年一次的亮相。

929
00:40:22.520 --> 00:40:22.960
Sam.
萨姆。

930
00:40:23.200 --> 00:40:24.100
So many questions.
有太多的问题了。

931
00:40:24.380 --> 00:40:24.740
So many questions.
