00:53:49.680 --> 00:53:51.640
I've saged my place before.
我以前用鼠尾草熏过我的住处。

1235
00:53:51.640 --> 00:53:52.600
I've done a sage.
我熏过。

1236
00:53:52.760 --> 00:53:57.080
When I bought my house, I walked around and I saged it.
我买房的时候，拿着鼠尾草到处走，熏了整个房子。

1237
00:53:57.280 --> 00:54:00.480
I still have a ghost, but she's friendly, so I'm okay with it.
我家里现在还有一个鬼，不过她挺友善的，所以我倒不介意。

1238
00:54:00.920 --> 00:54:04.700
I've had hippie woo-woo friends come over and sage my places for me.
我曾让那些信奉新时代玄学的朋友来过家里，帮我用鼠尾草净化过。

1239
00:54:05.280 --> 00:54:05.440
Yeah.
对。

1240
00:54:05.900 --> 00:54:06.580
Same, Sam.
我也是，萨姆。

1241
00:54:06.840 --> 00:54:09.960
One of my friends came over when I bought my house because it's an older house,
我买房的时候，我有个朋友过来，因为那是一栋老房子，

1242
00:54:09.960 --> 00:54:12.020
and she's like, well, first of all, we're going to sage it.
她就说，首先，我们得用鼠尾草熏一下。

1243
00:54:12.260 --> 00:54:13.440
So she did that.
于是她就照做了。

1244
00:54:13.620 --> 00:54:15.640
A week later, my mom and sister came out.
一个星期后，我妈和我姐过来了。

1245
00:54:15.800 --> 00:54:16.820
They prayed over the house.
她们为房子作了祈祷。

1246
00:54:17.080 --> 00:54:18.700
So I've got everything covered.
所以我这算是双管齐下了。

1247
00:54:18.920 --> 00:54:19.140
Yeah.
对。

1248
00:54:19.760 --> 00:54:20.400
That's good.
那挺好的。

1249
00:54:20.640 --> 00:54:20.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1250
00:54:21.400 --> 00:54:23.620
I think everywhere I live, I'm going to do both things.
我想我以后不管住在哪里，这两样都会做一遍。

1251
00:54:24.020 --> 00:54:24.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1252
00:54:24.880 --> 00:54:25.540
Might as well.
也行。

1253
00:54:25.640 --> 00:54:26.180
Might as well.
也行。

1254
00:54:26.500 --> 00:54:26.960
Right?
对吧？

1255
00:54:27.200 --> 00:54:28.740
Good energy only here, people.
各位，这里只要正能量。

1256
00:54:29.340 --> 00:54:29.900
Agree.
同意。

1257
00:54:31.080 --> 00:54:37.560
So we're back in the car, and Mare is finishing talking to this writer from the Cleveland paper,
所以我们回到车上，梅尔正跟克利夫兰报社的一个记者通完话，

1258
00:54:39.120 --> 00:54:47.440
and it really bumps Ned because basically Mare says to the writer how hands-off Ned is as the editor,
这让内德很不爽，因为基本上梅尔对记者说内德这个主编当得有多甩手，

1259
00:54:47.440 --> 00:54:50.080
that she can just basically do whatever she wants.
说她基本上想干什么就干什么。

1260
00:54:50.800 --> 00:54:56.040
And he starts to say something, but then Mare is done with the conversation, hangs up the phone.
他刚想说点什么，但梅尔已经结束了对话，挂了电话。

1261
00:54:56.360 --> 00:54:59.940
I mean, she's intending it as a compliment because the writer is like,
我的意思是，她本意是夸奖，因为那个记者说，

1262
00:55:00.080 --> 00:55:06.080
I'm surprised that with your paper's affiliation with Softies that you were able to write this
我很惊讶，凭你们报社和软心饼干的关联，你竟然能写出这篇文章，

1263
00:55:06.080 --> 00:55:08.280
article, and she's like, oh, no, no, no, my editor.
然后她就说，哦，不，不，不，我的主编。

1264
00:55:08.500 --> 00:55:09.400
He's very hands-off.
他非常放权。

1265
00:55:09.820 --> 00:55:14.520
She makes a comment where she's like, I mean, I think the readers read the article before he did.
她还随口说了一句，意思是，我觉得读者看文章的时候，他都还没看过。

1266
00:55:14.840 --> 00:55:16.140
That's what really gets him.
这才是真正惹恼他的地方。

1267
00:55:16.240 --> 00:55:16.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1268
00:55:16.380 --> 00:55:20.720
Because then he doesn't seem hands-off, like letting his reporters really have integrity.
因为这样一来，就不像是放权让记者真正有独立性了。

1269
00:55:20.720 --> 00:55:24.000
Then it seems like he's just half-assing it.
倒显得他纯粹是在敷衍了事。

1270
00:55:24.620 --> 00:55:24.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1271
00:55:25.300 --> 00:55:28.260
So they stop at a diner on their way.
所以他们在路上去了一家餐馆。

1272
00:55:28.420 --> 00:55:30.080
They haven't gotten to the cult place yet.
他们还没到那个邪教的地方。

1273
00:55:30.240 --> 00:55:32.920
They stop at a diner, and Ned decides, you know what?
他们在一个餐馆停下，然后内德决定，你知道吗？

1274
00:55:32.920 --> 00:55:34.240
Ned, I want to review your questions.
内德，我想过目一下你的问题。

1275
00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:39.240
He's decided suddenly to take an interest in these questions she might ask.
他突然决定开始关心她可能会问的这些问题。

1276
00:55:39.480 --> 00:55:41.200
Because he had no interest before.
因为他之前一点兴趣也没有。

1277
00:55:41.400 --> 00:55:41.700
Exactly.
没错。

1278
00:55:41.700 --> 00:55:42.860
He was like, I trust you.
他当时的态度是，我相信你。

1279
00:55:43.040 --> 00:55:47.320
Well, now he gets out a pen, a red pen, and he's like marking up the document.
好了，现在他掏出一支笔，红笔，开始在文件上涂涂改改。

1280
00:55:47.640 --> 00:55:47.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1281
00:55:48.860 --> 00:55:52.600
Mare does have a throwaway line here where she looks out the window and says,
梅尔在这里随口说了一句，她看着窗外说道，

1282
00:55:53.240 --> 00:55:56.780
I think my dad took me to a pencil sharpener museum around here.
我记得我爸以前带我参观过附近的一个转笔刀博物馆。

1283
00:55:57.480 --> 00:55:58.140
Oh, yeah.
哦，真的吗。

1284
00:55:58.140 --> 00:56:01.420
I mean, come on, a pencil sharpener museum?
我的天，转笔刀博物馆？

1285
00:56:01.620 --> 00:56:02.440
Wait, is that real?
等等，那是真的吗？

1286
00:56:02.660 --> 00:56:03.580
It's real.
是真的。

1287
00:56:03.820 --> 00:56:04.780
Stop everything.
停下所有事。

1288
00:56:05.120 --> 00:56:05.680
It is real.
千真万确。

1289
00:56:06.180 --> 00:56:08.780
Yes, I had to be a lady who Googled again.
没错，我又得当那个去谷歌搜索的女士了。

1290
00:56:09.540 --> 00:56:10.760
This is so fun.
这太有趣了。

1291
00:56:10.920 --> 00:56:13.820
There is a pencil sharpener museum in Logan, Ohio.
俄亥俄州洛根市真的有一个转笔刀博物馆。

1292
00:56:14.360 --> 00:56:15.860
And I went to the website.
我甚至去看了他们的网站。

1293
00:56:16.080 --> 00:56:16.960
Here's what it says.
上面是这么写的。

1294
00:56:17.200 --> 00:56:22.940
Stop by the Hocking Hills Regional Welcome Center and visit one of the more unique museums you will see.
欢迎光临霍金山地区迎宾中心，参观您将见过的最独特的博物馆之一。

1295
00:56:23.200 --> 00:56:24.260
The Paul A.
保罗·A·

1296
00:56:24.440 --> 00:56:26.380
Johnson Pencil Sharpener Museum.
约翰逊转笔刀博物馆。

1297
00:56:26.380 --> 00:56:30.500
Reverend Paul Johnson began his collection more than 20 years ago.
保罗·约翰逊牧师在20多年前开始了他的收藏。

1298
00:56:30.720 --> 00:56:35.860
It has over 3,400 pencil sharpeners, featured in national magazines.
它拥有3400多件转笔刀，曾登上各大国家级杂志。

1299
00:56:35.860 --> 00:56:38.880
It's reputed to be the largest collection in America.
据称这是全美最大的收藏。

1300
00:56:39.080 --> 00:56:42.140
And recently, they added Frank Parade's collection.
最近，他们还加入了弗兰克·帕雷德的藏品。

1301
00:56:42.440 --> 00:56:47.680
And with those combined collections, there's an estimated 5,000 pencil sharpeners.
结合这两处藏品，估计大约有5000个卷笔刀。

1302
00:56:48.760 --> 00:56:50.060
And there's pictures.
而且还有照片。

1303
00:56:50.340 --> 00:56:53.980
You wouldn't believe the different types of pencil sharpeners.
你绝对想不到卷笔刀有这么多不同的种类。

1304
00:56:54.120 --> 00:56:55.440
It's fascinating to me.
这对我来说太迷人了。

1305
00:56:55.440 --> 00:57:01.160
I am actually feeling angry right now that I am 52 years old almoSt.
我其实现在觉得挺生气的，因为我都快52岁了。

1306
00:57:01.480 --> 00:57:04.440
And I'm only just learning about this pencil sharpener museum.
而我居然才知道这个卷笔刀博物馆的存在。

1307
00:57:05.300 --> 00:57:06.400
Like, what?
简直了，什么情况？

1308
00:57:06.820 --> 00:57:08.260
I need to go there.
我得去一趟。

1309
00:57:08.420 --> 00:57:09.500
Like, soon.
就快点去。

1310
00:57:09.740 --> 00:57:11.020
Do you love a pencil sharpener?
你喜欢卷笔刀吗？

1311
00:57:11.580 --> 00:57:12.140
No.
不喜欢。

1312
00:57:12.380 --> 00:57:16.400
I love museums of tiny things like pencil sharpeners.
我喜欢微型物品的博物馆，比如卷笔刀。

1313
00:57:16.400 --> 00:57:17.940
Well, I love a pencil sharpener.
好吧，我很喜欢卷笔刀。

1314
00:57:17.980 --> 00:57:20.200
I love the randomness of this collection.
我喜欢这个收藏的随性劲儿。

1315
00:57:20.600 --> 00:57:22.580
There's pictures on the website, you guys.
官网上有照片，伙计们。

1316
00:57:22.780 --> 00:57:23.980
I'll share it in stories.
我会发到快拍里分享的。

1317
00:57:23.980 --> 00:57:29.300
Well, now Ned and Mare are going to arrive at the Fertile Soil Farm Collective.
好了，现在内德和梅尔要到达肥沃土壤农场集体了。

1318
00:57:30.060 --> 00:57:31.800
And the camera crew can't come with them.
而且摄像团队不能跟他们一起去。

1319
00:57:32.080 --> 00:57:32.840
They have to stay back.
他们必须留在后面。

1320
00:57:33.120 --> 00:57:33.340
Yeah.
对。

1321
00:57:33.420 --> 00:57:34.280
Mare says, quote,
梅尔说，原话是，

1322
00:57:34.420 --> 00:57:37.900
the cult dude is kind of secretive in an on-brand way.
那个邪教头子神神秘秘的，倒挺符合他人设的。

1323
00:57:38.660 --> 00:57:45.040
So, they walk up, the cameras stay back, but you can see people are all kind of doing yard work.
所以，他们走过去，摄像机留在后面，但你能看到大家都在做园艺活。

1324
00:57:45.040 --> 00:57:48.120
They're raking, and they're all wearing these red ponchos.
他们在扫树叶，而且每个人都穿着红色的雨披。

1325
00:57:48.520 --> 00:57:49.940
Yeah, matching ponchos.
对，配套的雨披。

1326
00:57:50.240 --> 00:57:55.060
I noted that Ned still has his yellow backpack from when we first met him in the first episode.
我注意到内德还背着他在第一集我们刚见他时的那个黄色双肩包。

1327
00:57:55.060 --> 00:57:56.740
I thought that was a nice callback.
我觉得这是一个很棒的呼应。

1328
00:57:57.660 --> 00:58:00.440
Um, I have a missed opportunity alert here.
嗯，我这里有一个错过良机的警报。

1329
00:58:00.640 --> 00:58:00.940
Okay.
好。

1330
00:58:02.380 --> 00:58:08.100
How great would it have been if just one of the people in a red poncho was Creed?
如果穿红雨披的人里哪怕只有一个人是克里德，那该有多棒啊？

1331
00:58:08.720 --> 00:58:09.280
Yes.
没错。

1332
00:58:09.880 --> 00:58:10.960
Come on.
拜托。

1333
00:58:11.140 --> 00:58:11.860
Right, Sam?
对吧，萨姆？

1334
00:58:12.140 --> 00:58:12.700
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1335
00:58:13.420 --> 00:58:13.980
Yes.
对。

1336
00:58:14.240 --> 00:58:14.540
Yeah.
对。

1337
00:58:14.740 --> 00:58:15.900
We don't hear from him.
我们听不到他的声音。

1338
00:58:16.440 --> 00:58:18.220
Still with the beard from the last episode.
还留着上一集的胡子。

1339
00:58:18.220 --> 00:58:20.280
Just a quick push in.
只是一个快速推镜头。

1340
00:58:20.480 --> 00:58:20.700
Yeah.
对。

1341
00:58:20.960 --> 00:58:22.500
He doesn't even have to say anything.
他甚至都不用说什么。

1342
00:58:22.760 --> 00:58:25.060
He's just raking some leaves with the other people.
他只是和其他人一起扫着落叶。

1343
00:58:25.260 --> 00:58:25.680
Exactly.
确实。

1344
00:58:26.080 --> 00:58:26.140
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1345
00:58:26.540 --> 00:58:28.640
Oh, that would have been great.
噢，那绝对太棒了。

1346
00:58:29.880 --> 00:58:33.020
I asked Dave Rogers, where did you shoot this?
我问戴夫·罗杰斯，你们在哪里拍的？

1347
00:58:33.620 --> 00:58:36.280
And he said it was the magic of filmmaking.
他说这就是电影制作的魅力。

1348
00:58:36.280 --> 00:58:42.900
They shot it on the Universal backlot at a place that was a house that had some good trees and some good brush around it.
他们在环球影城的片场外景地拍的，那里有一栋房子，周围有些很好的树木和灌木丛。

1349
00:58:43.060 --> 00:58:46.700
He said the art department did a great job making it look like a farm.
他说美术部门把这里装扮得像个农场，做得太棒了。

1350
00:58:46.700 --> 00:58:49.720
And I can't believe that this was shot on the lot.
我真不敢相信这竟然是在片场拍的。

1351
00:58:49.940 --> 00:58:52.200
This is like just blowing my mind.
这简直让我大开眼界。

1352
00:58:52.380 --> 00:58:54.480
I know we're kind of a broken record here.
我知道我们有点像老生常谈。

1353
00:58:54.600 --> 00:59:00.600
But you guys, when we went to Shroot Farms, we went to a freaking farm an hour outside of L.A.
但各位，当我们去舒鲁特农场时，我们去了一个离洛杉矶一小时车程的该死的农场。

1354
00:59:00.760 --> 00:59:04.420
We had to have a rattlesnake wrangler because there were rattlesnakes everywhere.
我们不得不请一个响尾蛇驯蛇师，因为到处都是响尾蛇。

1355
00:59:04.740 --> 00:59:06.960
We had to leave our houses at 430 in the morning.
我们不得不早上4点半离开家。

1356
00:59:07.220 --> 00:59:12.800
I mean, I guess that's what you get when you shoot on a big time real deal old Hollywood lot, which is amazing.
我的意思是，我想这就是在大牌真正的老好莱坞片场拍摄所能得到的待遇，太棒了。

1357
00:59:12.800 --> 00:59:19.180
They have all these different nooks and crannies that look like New York City or an old town square or a farm.
他们有各种各样的角角落落，看起来像纽约市、老城镇广场或农场。

1358
00:59:19.960 --> 00:59:24.200
And we just shot in this tiny soundstage in Van Nuys.
而我们却在范奈司的一个小小摄影棚里拍摄。

1359
00:59:24.300 --> 00:59:25.420
So we had to travel.
所以我们得四处奔波。

1360
00:59:25.660 --> 00:59:28.960
If we had to show any part of the world, we had to get out.
如果我们必须展示世界的任何部分，我们就得走出去。

1361
00:59:29.120 --> 00:59:31.500
We had to load up in a van and go on the road.
我们不得不装上一辆面包车上路。

1362
00:59:31.640 --> 00:59:33.060
And watch out for rattlesnakes.
还要小心响尾蛇。

1363
00:59:33.160 --> 00:59:33.360
Yep.
没错。

1364
00:59:34.300 --> 00:59:35.980
Or a bee in John's eggs.
或者约翰的鸡蛋里有只蜜蜂。

1365
00:59:36.800 --> 00:59:37.200
Correct.
没错。

1366
00:59:37.200 --> 00:59:44.740
Well, back at The Truth Teller, Oscar announces he has discovered who the troll is.
好了，回到《实话实说》节目，奥斯卡宣布他已经查出谁是喷子了。

1367
00:59:44.960 --> 00:59:47.800
I guess he called the IT department after all.
我想他终究还是给IT部门打了电话。

1368
00:59:47.900 --> 00:59:48.420
He did.
他确实打了。

1369
00:59:48.600 --> 00:59:49.380
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1370
00:59:49.700 --> 00:59:52.080
It's coming from inside the building.
它是从大楼内部发出的。

1371
00:59:52.800 --> 00:59:56.240
It's coming from Ann Putnam's office.
它是从安·帕特农的办公室发出的。

1372
00:59:56.540 --> 00:59:56.700
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1373
00:59:56.700 --> 00:59:59.540
Marv's assistant and sister-in-law, Ann.
马尔v的助理兼小姨子，安。

1374
00:59:59.800 --> 01:00:01.280
They cannot believe this.
他们简直不敢相信。

1375
01:00:01.280 --> 01:00:06.700
But Oscar has a talking head that's great, where he says it makes sense.
但奥斯卡有一个很棒的采访镜头，他说这说得通。

1376
01:00:06.880 --> 01:00:07.880
Let's hear it.
我们听听看。

1377
01:00:08.380 --> 01:00:11.440
I see it often in people over 50.
我在50岁以上的人身上经常看到这种现象。

1378
01:00:12.700 --> 01:00:15.420
They get trapped in the year that they join Facebook.
他们被困在了他们加入脸书的那一年。

1379
01:00:15.660 --> 01:00:19.340
It's as if the technology sends their brain into shock.
就好像这项技术让他们的的大脑受到了震惊。

1380
01:00:19.680 --> 01:00:22.660
And their online personalities get frozen in time.
他们的网络个性被时间冻结了。

1381
01:00:24.220 --> 01:00:30.120
So Ann is basically a snarky millennial trapped in the body of a boomer.
所以安基本上是一个被困在婴儿潮一代体内的尖酸刻薄的千禧一代。

1382
01:00:30.120 --> 01:00:32.340
That is such a funny description.
这个形容太有趣了。

1383
01:00:32.680 --> 01:00:34.440
I think there's some real truth in it.
我觉得其中确实有些真相。

1384
01:00:34.620 --> 01:00:35.760
There might be.
也许吧。

1385
01:00:36.120 --> 01:00:39.540
And look, I know my sister Janet listens to the podcaSt.
听着，我知道我姐姐珍妮特听这个播客。

1386
01:00:39.840 --> 01:00:48.460
But Janet, the emojis you use are very telling to me when you started having like the smartphone thing.
但珍妮特，你使用的表情符号清楚地表明了你大概是什么时候开始接触智能手机这种东西的。

1387
01:00:49.000 --> 01:00:49.340
Why?
为什么？

1388
01:00:49.700 --> 01:00:52.040
I only use a handful of emojis.
我只用少数几个表情符号。

1389
01:00:52.640 --> 01:00:56.740
And I think it's because early on there were only a few to choose from.
我想这是因为早期只有那么几个可供选择。

1390
01:00:56.900 --> 01:00:57.780
And now there's so many.
而现在有这么多了。

1391
01:00:57.780 --> 01:01:03.540
I only use facepalm, heart, and like the person who's crying while they laugh.
我只用捂脸、爱心，还有像笑得哭出来的那种表情。

1392
01:01:03.740 --> 01:01:09.200
See, I think that shows when you joined the sort of smartphone thing, right?
你看，我觉得这就暴露了你是什么时候加入智能手机大军的，对吧？

1393
01:01:10.220 --> 01:01:11.620
Sam, what about you?
萨姆，你呢？

1394
01:01:11.820 --> 01:01:13.800
I am partial to the guy giving the salute.
我比较喜欢那个敬礼的家伙。

1395
01:01:14.140 --> 01:01:14.700
Oh.
哦。

1396
01:01:14.780 --> 01:01:21.560
It's a good, I've heard your sentence, and I want to not give input to the conversation, wrap it up emoji.
这是一个“我听到了你的话，但不想对谈话发表意见，就这样结束吧”的表情符号。

1397
01:01:24.340 --> 01:01:28.980
I use the smiley face that has the like straight line smile of all teeth.
我用的是那个牙齿龇成一条直线微笑的笑脸。

1398
01:01:29.180 --> 01:01:29.540
Like, ooh.
就像，噢。

1399
01:01:29.800 --> 01:01:29.920
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1400
01:01:30.060 --> 01:01:30.340
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1401
01:01:30.800 --> 01:01:31.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1402
01:01:31.200 --> 01:01:34.200
Angela, I'm constantly using that one because I always feel that way.
安吉拉，我经常用那个，因为我一直都有那种感觉。

1403
01:01:34.380 --> 01:01:34.600
Yeah.
对。

1404
01:01:34.780 --> 01:01:35.160
Ooh.
噢。

1405
01:01:35.720 --> 01:01:38.140
Or I use the lady in the red dress running.
或者我用那个穿红裙子奔跑的女士。

1406
01:01:38.560 --> 01:01:39.680
Yeah, you love that one.
对，你超爱那个。

1407
01:01:39.720 --> 01:01:40.500
I love that one.
我很喜欢那个。

1408
01:01:40.500 --> 01:01:41.920
And four, that's like party.
还有第四个，那个就像是聚会。

1409
01:01:42.400 --> 01:01:45.000
I think it's just like, I'm a badass, I'm running my dress.
我觉得那就像是，我太酷了，我穿着裙子在奔跑。

1410
01:01:45.280 --> 01:01:46.180
And isn't she dancing?
她难道不是在跳舞吗？

1411
01:01:46.500 --> 01:01:47.460
I think she is.
我觉得她是。

1412
01:01:47.620 --> 01:01:59.060
But like my sister Janet will do like, like the hand emojis that's like thumbs up, then I love you, then peace, fingers, and then like a hamburger, a glass of wine, champagne.
但就像我姐姐珍妮特会发那种，就像是手势表情，先是竖起大拇指，然后我爱你，然后是V字手势，接着像是一个汉堡、一杯葡萄酒、香槟。

1413
01:01:59.500 --> 01:02:01.980
Well, the thumbs up just reads as passive aggressive.
嗯，竖大拇指看起来就像是带有被动攻击性。

1414
01:02:02.220 --> 01:02:02.840
That's like texting.
这就跟发短信一样。

1415
01:02:03.080 --> 01:02:04.220
No, she's not.
不，她没有。

1416
01:02:04.320 --> 01:02:05.460
She's not passive aggressive.
她没有被动攻击。

1417
01:02:06.060 --> 01:02:09.940
I was just reading how people want to cancel the thumbs up because people think it's passive aggressive.
我刚刚看到一篇报道说人们想取消竖大拇指，因为大家觉得它带有被动攻击性。

1418
01:02:09.940 --> 01:02:12.020
And I was like, oh, no, that's my most common one.
当时我想，哦，不，那是我最常用的一个。

1419
01:02:12.380 --> 01:02:14.040
Oh, I do thumbs up all the time.
哦，我一直都在用竖大拇指。

1420
01:02:14.160 --> 01:02:15.180
And I'm not used to me.
而且我不是针对我。

1421
01:02:15.280 --> 01:02:17.960
Me and my dad wouldn't talk if we didn't do thumbs up emojis.
要不是发竖大拇指表情，我和我爸根本就不会聊天。

1422
01:02:18.220 --> 01:02:18.600
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1423
01:02:18.840 --> 01:02:21.440
It's a perfect dad and son emoji.
这绝对是个完美的父子表情符号。

1424
01:02:21.640 --> 01:02:22.240
I'll give you that.
我承认这点。

1425
01:02:22.500 --> 01:02:22.760
Okay.
好吧。

1426
01:02:23.060 --> 01:02:23.460
Yeah.
对。

1427
01:02:24.560 --> 01:02:25.260
I don't know.
我不知道。

1428
01:02:25.260 --> 01:02:29.440
Maybe it's time to throw some new ones in our emoji resume, guys.
也许是时候在我们的表情符号库里加入一些新面孔了，伙计们。

1429
01:02:29.640 --> 01:02:30.080
You know what?
你知道吗？

1430
01:02:30.080 --> 01:02:33.060
I want to put this out there in our office ladies text thread.
我想在我们的“办公室女士”短信群里发这个。

1431
01:02:33.380 --> 01:02:35.640
Feel free to try on new emojis.
大家尽管尝试新的表情符号。

1432
01:02:35.680 --> 01:02:36.160
No judgment.
绝不评判。

1433
01:02:36.540 --> 01:02:36.720
Yeah.
对。

1434
01:02:36.880 --> 01:02:39.040
It's our safe space to try new things.
这是我们尝试新事物的安全港湾。

1435
01:02:39.140 --> 01:02:39.820
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1436
01:02:40.100 --> 01:02:40.980
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1437
01:02:41.200 --> 01:02:44.180
Well, now we're going to go back to a fertile soil.
好了，现在我们要回到那片肥沃的土地。

1438
01:02:45.040 --> 01:02:45.840
They're leaving.
他们要走了。

1439
01:02:46.020 --> 01:02:47.000
They're getting in their car.
他们上车了。

1440
01:02:48.020 --> 01:02:52.300
And Ned has decided they're not a cult.
内德已经认定他们不是一个邪教。

1441
01:02:52.900 --> 01:02:54.820
Mayor thinks they are a cult.
市长觉得他们是个邪教。

1442
01:02:54.820 --> 01:02:57.580
Mayor's like, you didn't let me ask any hard-hitting questions.
市长好像在说，你都不让我问任何尖锐的问题。

1443
01:02:57.580 --> 01:03:00.260
And they get in their car, and they're just annoyed with each other.
然后他们上车了，彼此都觉得很烦躁。

1444
01:03:00.440 --> 01:03:00.640
Yeah.
对。

1445
01:03:00.800 --> 01:03:04.640
And this back and forth about whether or not they're a cult or not follows them back onto
关于他们到底是不是邪教的争论一路伴随着他们

1446
01:03:04.640 --> 01:03:05.580
their drive home.
开车回家。

1447
01:03:05.760 --> 01:03:06.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1448
01:03:06.560 --> 01:03:09.500
It did make me wonder, could the right cult get you?
这确实让我纳闷，合适的邪教会把你拉拢进去吗？

1449
01:03:09.920 --> 01:03:12.660
This was a question Ned asks early on.
这是内德早期提出的一个问题。

1450
01:03:12.820 --> 01:03:13.140
Right.
没错。

1451
01:03:13.380 --> 01:03:17.220
Because I kind of joined a cult once on accident.
因为我曾经不小心加入过一个邪教。

1452
01:03:18.360 --> 01:03:18.840
And...
然后……

1453
01:03:18.840 --> 01:03:23.320
Being your friend all these years, I want to say this is really on brand.
跟你做朋友这么多年，我想说这真的很符合你的人设。

1454
01:03:23.320 --> 01:03:29.100
I think when people first meet us, Sam, maybe you would think I'm the one that would fall
我想当人们第一次见到我们时，萨姆，也许你会觉得我是那种会落入

1455
01:03:29.100 --> 01:03:29.960
prey to a cult.
邪教圈套的人。

1456
01:03:30.280 --> 01:03:31.500
No, not at all.
不，完全不是。

1457
01:03:31.600 --> 01:03:32.460
Actually, Jenna.
其实是珍娜。

1458
01:03:33.900 --> 01:03:38.420
Well, this is also how I accidentally joined a call girl ring.
好吧，这也是我怎么不小心加入了一个应召女郎团伙的经历。

1459
01:03:38.580 --> 01:03:39.000
Yes.
是的。

1460
01:03:39.140 --> 01:03:41.600
Because I thought I had joined a singing group.
因为我以为我加入了一个歌唱团体。

1461
01:03:42.040 --> 01:03:42.520
Yes.
是的。

1462
01:03:42.520 --> 01:03:46.700
You're oddly, like, very susceptible to these groups.
你呢，就很奇怪地非常容易受这些团体蛊惑。

1463
01:03:46.920 --> 01:03:47.560
I am.
我是这样的。

1464
01:03:47.980 --> 01:03:48.420
Yeah.
对啊。

1465
01:03:48.760 --> 01:03:50.740
And you're such a critical thinker.
而你明明是个这么有批判性思维的人。

1466
01:03:50.860 --> 01:03:51.240
I know.
我知道。

1467
01:03:51.460 --> 01:03:55.600
And yet, I also believe a ghost lives in my closet, lady.
然而，我还坚信我的衣橱里住着一个鬼魂呢，大姐。

1468
01:03:55.800 --> 01:03:56.600
I don't know.
我不知道。

1469
01:03:56.900 --> 01:04:01.420
Well, lady, if you ever get sucked in by a cult, I'd come and get you.
好吧，大姐，如果你哪天被邪教给骗进去了，我会去救你的。

1470
01:04:01.720 --> 01:04:02.340
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1471
01:04:02.340 --> 01:04:03.680
I know that you will.
我知道你会的。

1472
01:04:03.900 --> 01:04:04.500
You're welcome.
不客气。

1473
01:04:04.760 --> 01:04:05.680
That's best friendship.
这才是真正的友谊。

1474
01:04:05.880 --> 01:04:06.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1475
01:04:06.160 --> 01:04:10.440
Well, now, as they're arguing and driving down the road, Mare gets a flat tire.
好了，现在，当他们在车里边吵架边开车时，梅尔的车胎爆了。

1476
01:04:11.200 --> 01:04:11.600
Yes.
对。

1477
01:04:12.080 --> 01:04:13.820
They're going to have to change this tire.
他们得换个轮胎了。

1478
01:04:14.000 --> 01:04:15.100
Mare is going to change it.
梅尔打算去换胎。

1479
01:04:15.220 --> 01:04:17.640
Ned's just, like, sitting in the back of the trunk.
内德就那样坐在后备箱里。

1480
01:04:17.820 --> 01:04:22.660
Like, do you know how hard it is to ratchet up your car in the first place, and he's just
就好像，你知道一开始要把车顶起来有多难吗，而他居然就

1481
01:04:22.660 --> 01:04:23.700
sitting in the back?
坐在后面？

1482
01:04:23.840 --> 01:04:24.460
Oh, yeah.
哦，对啊。

1483
01:04:24.720 --> 01:04:25.520
What the heck, Ned?
搞什么鬼，内德？

1484
01:04:25.680 --> 01:04:26.540
What the heck, Ned?
搞什么鬼，内德？

1485
01:04:27.120 --> 01:04:29.000
I do have a wardrobe catch here.
我这里发现了一个服装穿帮。

1486
01:04:29.300 --> 01:04:29.900
What is it?
是什么？

1487
01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:31.680
15 minutes, 25 seconds.
15分25秒。

1488
01:04:31.900 --> 01:04:35.400
I absolutely loved the boots that Mare's wearing.
我太喜欢梅尔穿的那双靴子了。

1489
01:04:35.400 --> 01:04:37.100
So, I had to Google them.
所以，我不得不去谷歌了一下。

1490
01:04:37.260 --> 01:04:41.100
I went on to one of the websites I use to check costume and wardrobe stuff.
我上了我平时用来查戏服和服装的网站之一。

1491
01:04:42.700 --> 01:04:48.880
ShopYourTV.com says they are the six-inch classic mock women's short boot in black boundary
ShopYourTV.com 上说那是红翼牌的黑色经典莫卡辛女士短靴，皮质是 Black Boundary

1492
01:04:48.880 --> 01:04:50.040
leather by Red Wing.
皮革。

1493
01:04:50.720 --> 01:04:52.100
Oh, are they expensive?
哦，它们很贵吗？

1494
01:04:52.320 --> 01:04:58.220
They retail for $319.99, but they are really cool looking.
零售价是 319.99 美元，但它们看起来真的很酷。

1495
01:04:58.440 --> 01:04:59.040
You want to see?
你想看看吗？

1496
01:04:59.340 --> 01:04:59.580
Yeah.
好啊。

1497
01:05:01.320 --> 01:05:03.040
Oh, those are super cool.
哦，那些超级酷。

1498
01:05:03.280 --> 01:05:03.880
I know.
我知道。

1499
01:05:04.020 --> 01:05:04.220
Yeah.
对啊。

1500
01:05:04.880 --> 01:05:06.380
Those are really cool.
那些真的很酷。

1501
01:05:06.580 --> 01:05:07.000
I know.
我知道。

1502
01:05:07.120 --> 01:05:08.180
I kind of want a pair now.
我现在甚至有点想买一双了。

1503
01:05:08.340 --> 01:05:11.440
If I were Chelsea, I would ask to take those home at the end of the season.
要我是切尔西，季末我就会要求把那些带回家。

1504
01:05:11.540 --> 01:05:12.580
I hope she gets them.
我希望她能如愿以偿。

1505
01:05:12.860 --> 01:05:15.740
Well, I asked Dave Rogers where they shot this, and guess what?
我问过戴夫·罗杰斯他们是在哪里拍的，你猜怎么着？

1506
01:05:16.020 --> 01:05:17.980
Also on the Universal backlot.
也是在环球影城的片场外景地。

1507
01:05:18.200 --> 01:05:24.740
They found a street on the lot just right around the corner from that house that was being the
他们在片场找到了一条街，就在那个农舍的拐角

1508
01:05:24.740 --> 01:05:25.160
farm.
附近。

1509
01:05:25.160 --> 01:05:27.620
And I mean, this is crazy.
我是说，这太疯狂了。

1510
01:05:27.920 --> 01:05:33.300
This street on the Universal backlot had a hill because Mare's going to get mad at Ned,
环球影城外景地的这条街居然有个坡，因为梅尔要生内德的气，

1511
01:05:33.440 --> 01:05:37.720
and she's going to roll the tire down this hill and make him chase after it.
她要把轮胎顺着这个坡滚下去，让他去追。

1512
01:05:37.880 --> 01:05:40.080
I can't believe that was on the Universal backlot.
我真不敢相信那是环球影城外景地拍的。

1513
01:05:40.120 --> 01:05:40.580
I can't either.
我也这么觉得。

1514
01:05:40.780 --> 01:05:42.000
That lot is huge, though.
不过那个片场可太大了。

1515
01:05:42.200 --> 01:05:43.260
It goes on and on.
简直无边无际。

1516
01:05:43.460 --> 01:05:43.980
Well, this is true.
好吧，这倒是真的。

1517
01:05:44.520 --> 01:05:46.340
Well, now here's a moment of truth.
好了，现在到了见证真相的时刻。

1518
01:05:46.340 --> 01:05:51.400
Because Oscar and the rest of the gang are going to go confront Anne about her snarky
因为奥斯卡和其他人要去质问安关于她那些尖酸

1519
01:05:51.400 --> 01:05:52.080
comments.
刻薄的评论。

1520
01:05:52.260 --> 01:05:52.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1521
01:05:53.440 --> 01:05:56.940
And the character of Anne could win a little Oscar here.
安这个角色在这里简直能拿个小金人。

1522
01:05:57.200 --> 01:05:58.260
She really could.
她真的可以。

1523
01:05:58.480 --> 01:05:59.340
She's like, what?
她装得像是在说，什么？

1524
01:05:59.680 --> 01:06:01.460
Who would do such awful things?
谁会做出这么过分的事？

1525
01:06:01.580 --> 01:06:03.240
And then she's like, oh, dang it.
然后她又说，哦，该死。

1526
01:06:03.680 --> 01:06:06.180
Marv has told me I need to set a password.
马尔夫提醒过我要设置密码。

1527
01:06:06.200 --> 01:06:10.340
And I just thought, who would ever just come on my computer and do something like that?
我当时就在想，谁会无缘无故登录我的电脑做这种事呢？

1528
01:06:10.460 --> 01:06:11.920
I just feel horrible.
我真是太难过了。

1529
01:06:12.340 --> 01:06:14.100
And they're just like, oh, no, it's okay.
然后他们就说，哦，不，没事的。

1530
01:06:14.260 --> 01:06:14.720
It's okay.
没事的。

1531
01:06:14.720 --> 01:06:18.780
I know she's like, they shouldn't give people my age, these machines.
我知道，她就像在说，他们真不该给像我这个年纪的人用这些机器。

1532
01:06:19.220 --> 01:06:19.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1533
01:06:20.080 --> 01:06:23.940
She completely convinces them that she had nothing to do with it.
她彻底说服了他们，让他们觉得这事跟她一点关系都没有。

1534
01:06:24.220 --> 01:06:25.640
And they all leave.
然后他们全都走了。

1535
01:06:25.800 --> 01:06:29.020
And then she has this talking head where she says, you know what?
接着她对着镜头访谈说道，你知道吗？

1536
01:06:29.960 --> 01:06:34.800
Whoever the troll is probably just wants to hold the truth teller to a high standard of quality.
那个喷子可能只是想对说真话的人保持高标准的要求。

1537
01:06:35.600 --> 01:06:37.620
Marv has invested a lot of money.
马尔夫投资了好多钱呢。

1538
01:06:37.720 --> 01:06:40.560
So they need to make sure it's awesome sauce.
所以他们得确保这节目棒极了。

1539
01:06:40.960 --> 01:06:42.380
So it is Anne.
所以就是安干的。

1540
01:06:42.520 --> 01:06:43.360
It is Anne.
确实是安。

1541
01:06:43.360 --> 01:06:45.240
Do you think she'll keep doing it?
你觉得她还会继续这么做吗？

1542
01:06:45.740 --> 01:06:47.100
Yeah, I do.
会，我觉会的。

1543
01:06:47.240 --> 01:06:47.720
I do too.
我也这么觉得。

1544
01:06:48.540 --> 01:06:54.460
Well, Ned and Mare have changed their tire and they're stopping at this diner again on their way home.
好了，内德和梅尔换好轮胎，在回家的路上又在一家餐馆停了下来。

1545
01:06:55.580 --> 01:06:57.960
Ned tries to make a peace offering to Mare.
内德试图向梅尔示好求和。

1546
01:06:58.260 --> 01:07:00.160
He gets her this ice cream float.
他给她买了一杯冰淇淋汽水。

1547
01:07:00.660 --> 01:07:03.760
But he only buys one and it's only for Mare.
但他只买了一杯，而且是专门给梅尔的。

1548
01:07:03.760 --> 01:07:14.700
And so they get in this crazy, weird fight about who should eat this ice cream soda and go back and forth about it.
于是他们为这杯冰淇淋汽水到底该谁吃而吵得不可开交，推来推去。

1549
01:07:14.860 --> 01:07:15.740
It's very childish.
非常幼稚。

1550
01:07:16.240 --> 01:07:16.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1551
01:07:16.740 --> 01:07:16.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1552
01:07:16.980 --> 01:07:22.900
Dave shared that there was a fun bit of improv during this scene that he wished would have made it in.
戴夫分享说，这场戏里有一个很有趣的即兴发挥，他本来希望能够剪进正片里。

1553
01:07:23.620 --> 01:07:29.180
There was this moment, I guess, where Donal improvised actually eating the ice cream float.
我记得有这样一个瞬间，唐纳尔即兴表演了真的去吃那个冰淇淋苏打。

1554
01:07:29.580 --> 01:07:31.500
Like, he's like, fine, Mare, I'll eat it.
就好像，他说，好吧，玛尔，我吃。

1555
01:07:31.500 --> 01:07:34.580
And he downs it in, like, four spoonfuls.
然后他大概四勺就把它全吃光了。

1556
01:07:34.660 --> 01:07:36.220
And then Mare is shocked.
接着玛尔惊呆了。

1557
01:07:36.900 --> 01:07:40.260
And then he continues to try to make his case with her.
然后他继续试图向她陈述自己的观点。

1558
01:07:40.380 --> 01:07:42.560
But he has to stop because he has brain freeze.
但他不得不停下来，因为他脑子冻住了（头疼）。

1559
01:07:43.900 --> 01:07:45.940
Dave said it was such good improv.
戴夫说这真是一段极好的即兴表演。

1560
01:07:45.940 --> 01:07:47.260
He thought it was so funny.
他觉得太搞笑了。

1561
01:07:47.260 --> 01:07:49.140
He put it in his director's cut.
他把它放进了他的导演剪辑版里。

1562
01:07:49.340 --> 01:07:51.380
But ultimately, it got taken out.
但最终，它还是被删掉了。

1563
01:07:51.620 --> 01:07:52.060
Aw.
噢。

1564
01:07:52.060 --> 01:07:53.280
But he loved it.
但他很喜欢。

1565
01:07:53.680 --> 01:07:56.880
Maybe they'll get to do superfan versions of the paper.
也许他们以后能出报纸的超级粉丝剪辑版吧。

1566
01:07:57.520 --> 01:07:59.440
Superfan versions of the peacock version?
孔雀频道的超级粉丝剪辑版？

1567
01:07:59.600 --> 01:07:59.940
Yes.
对。

1568
01:08:00.240 --> 01:08:01.400
They can add even more?
他们还能加入更多内容吗？

1569
01:08:01.600 --> 01:08:01.800
Yeah.
是的。

1570
01:08:02.440 --> 01:08:05.300
Well, Ned and Mare are still bickering and they're back in the parking lot now.
好吧，内德和玛尔还在斗嘴，他们现在回到了停车场。

1571
01:08:05.400 --> 01:08:07.160
They're going to get in the car to drive back home.
他们要上车开车回家了。

1572
01:08:07.320 --> 01:08:14.960
When Ned gets a phone call, it's Detrick calling to tell them they were nominated for the Ohio Journalism Awards.
就在内德接到一个电话时，是迪特里克打来的，告诉他们获得了俄亥俄州新闻奖的提名。

1573
01:08:15.420 --> 01:08:15.860
Yes.
太棒了。

1574
01:08:16.440 --> 01:08:19.700
Mare is nominated for her Softies clogs Toledo story.
玛尔因她关于托莱多“舒适木屐鞋”的报道获得了提名。

1575
01:08:19.700 --> 01:08:24.260
But the entire paper is up for the overall excellence in journalism.
但整张报纸都入围了新闻业杰出综合奖。

1576
01:08:25.100 --> 01:08:26.740
And they are just elated.
他们简直欣喜若狂。

1577
01:08:26.980 --> 01:08:27.320
Yes.
是的。

1578
01:08:27.420 --> 01:08:30.140
They do a little happy dance in the parking lot.
他们在停车场高兴地跳起了一支庆祝舞。

1579
01:08:30.740 --> 01:08:32.640
So I guess all is forgiven there.
所以我想那里的恩怨都一笔勾销了。

1580
01:08:33.000 --> 01:08:35.280
I mean, this is very exciting.
我是说，这太令人兴奋了。

1581
01:08:35.560 --> 01:08:36.100
Big news.
大新闻。

1582
01:08:36.280 --> 01:08:36.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1583
01:08:36.980 --> 01:08:42.700
And you know, the next episode, the season finale, is the Ohio Journalism Awards.
你知道吗，下一集，也就是季终集，就是俄亥俄州新闻奖颁奖典礼了。

1584
01:08:43.080 --> 01:08:45.200
We're going to see how this all plays out.
我们将拭目以待这一切将如何发展。

1585
01:08:46.100 --> 01:08:55.680
But this episode is going to end with Esmeralda walking into the office and she just walks over to Barry's desk and she just gives him a big kiss on the lips.
但这一集的结尾是埃斯梅拉达走进了办公室，她径直走到巴里的桌子旁，狠狠地吻了他的嘴唇。

1586
01:08:56.000 --> 01:08:56.400
Yes.
没错。

1587
01:08:56.620 --> 01:09:01.620
And then she says this whole speech where she's like, you have been kissed on the 17th day of the month.
然后她发表了一长串演讲，大致意思是，你在本月的第十七天被吻了。

1588
01:09:01.760 --> 01:09:03.300
I command you to forsake me.
我命令你抛弃我。

1589
01:09:03.460 --> 01:09:03.880
Set me free.
放我自由。

1590
01:09:04.000 --> 01:09:04.400
Set me free.
放我自由。

1591
01:09:04.520 --> 01:09:04.980
Set me free.
放我自由。

1592
01:09:04.980 --> 01:09:07.160
And then she's like, the spell is broken.
接着她说，魔咒解除了。

1593
01:09:07.800 --> 01:09:09.680
And Barry's like, okay.
而巴里的反应是，好吧。

1594
01:09:11.200 --> 01:09:12.560
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

1595
01:09:13.200 --> 01:09:15.760
One last thing I want to share from Dave Rogers.
还有最后一件事我想分享，来自戴夫·罗杰斯。

1596
01:09:15.760 --> 01:09:17.200
I thought this was so sweet.
我觉得这太温馨了。

1597
01:09:17.560 --> 01:09:26.300
He said one of the highlights of the week of him directing this episode was that they got some very extra special VIPs that came to set.
他说他执导这一集的那周最精彩的亮点之一，就是有一些非常特别的贵宾来到了片场。

1598
01:09:26.780 --> 01:09:27.840
Jenna, you mentioned this.
珍娜，你提过这个。

1599
01:09:28.180 --> 01:09:30.360
These are Dave's words, not ours.
这是戴夫的原话，可不是我们说的。

1600
01:09:30.360 --> 01:09:38.860
He said the lovely Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey, who I might add, got a huge round of applause from the cast and crew when they stepped onto the set.
他说，可爱的珍娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金斯利——我要补充一句，当她们踏上片场时，受到了演员和剧组人员的热烈掌声。

1601
01:09:39.220 --> 01:09:42.920
Some of the cast told me later they were both excited and nervous to meet you.
有些演员后来告诉我，他们见到你们时既兴奋又紧张。

1602
01:09:43.200 --> 01:09:45.380
But it was so nice having you guys there.
但有你们在真的太好了。

1603
01:09:45.560 --> 01:09:53.900
And those of us who worked on The Office, like Greg, Rusty, Kelly, Keisha, Veda, Steve, and Lori, and Sergio, and of course Oscar,
而我们这些曾参与制作《办公室》的人，像格雷格、拉斯蒂、凯利、基莎、维达、史蒂夫、洛瑞、塞尔吉奥，当然还有奥斯卡，

1604
01:09:54.120 --> 01:09:56.800
were really thrilled and so happy to see you guys.
看到你们真的非常兴奋和高兴。

1605
01:09:57.060 --> 01:09:57.500
Aw.
噢。

1606
01:09:58.020 --> 01:09:59.360
That was really special.
那真的很特别。

1607
01:09:59.360 --> 01:10:00.780
We both teared up.
我们俩都感动得落泪了。

1608
01:10:00.940 --> 01:10:04.060
It was such a great group of people.
这真是一群很棒的人。

1609
01:10:05.000 --> 01:10:12.500
Well, you guys, thank you so much for listening to today's episode and for sending in your questions, your comments, your chit-chats, your around-the-towns.
好了，各位，非常感谢大家收听今天的节目，感谢大家发来你们的问题、评论、闲聊以及街头巷尾的趣闻。

1610
01:10:12.640 --> 01:10:17.480
And, of course, a huge thank you to Dave Rogers for giving us behind-the-scenes details.
当然，非常感谢戴夫·罗杰斯为我们提供幕后细节。

1611
01:10:17.920 --> 01:10:25.920
Dave would like you to know that the Season 9 Superfan episodes of The Office are up on Peacock right now.
戴夫想让大家知道，《办公室》第九季的超级粉丝版现已在Peacock上上线。

1612
01:10:25.920 --> 01:10:27.780
You know, he works so hard on them.
你知道的，他为这些付出了很多心血。

1613
01:10:28.120 --> 01:10:30.680
And we're going to talk more about those in a few episodes.
我们会在接下来的几期节目中更多地聊聊这些。

1614
01:10:30.720 --> 01:10:32.120
But they're really special.
但它们真的很特别。

1615
01:10:33.000 --> 01:10:36.120
And, of course, a big thank you to Chelsea Fry.
当然，还要非常感谢切尔西·弗莱。

1616
01:10:36.520 --> 01:10:37.140
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1617
01:10:37.140 --> 01:10:38.740
We loved watching you in this episode.
我们很喜欢看你在这一集里的表现。

1618
01:10:38.960 --> 01:10:41.580
Thanks for always texting us back when we DM you.
谢谢你每次我们给你发私信时都会回复。

1619
01:10:42.900 --> 01:10:44.040
All right, everyone.
好了，各位。

1620
01:10:44.040 --> 01:10:44.920
We love you.
我们爱你们。

1621
01:10:45.100 --> 01:10:47.060
And we will see you next week.
我们下周见。

1622
01:10:47.180 --> 01:10:53.920
And we should mention that next week we'll be breaking down the finale episode of The Paper with Chelsea Fry.
我们还要提一下，下周我们将和切尔西·弗莱一起剖析《纸业公司》的大结局。

1623
01:10:54.360 --> 01:10:55.180
In the studio.
在演播室里。

1624
01:10:55.180 --> 01:10:57.640
Yeah, so be sure to join us for that one.
对，所以千万别错过那一期。

1625
01:10:57.820 --> 01:10:58.320
We love you guys.
我们爱你们，伙计们。

1626
01:10:58.460 --> 01:10:59.060
See you next week.
下周见。

1627
01:10:59.160 --> 01:10:59.560
See you then.
到时见。

1628
01:11:02.780 --> 01:11:04.760
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

